                          "text":  "I am small. I weigh less than a big bottle of water, and I rode to Mars tucked under the belly of a rover the size of a car. My whole job was to answer one question: can anything fly here?\n\nIt was a fair question. The air on Mars is about a hundred times thinner than the air on Earth. There is almost nothing for a blade to push against. So my two rotors spin in opposite directions, incredibly fast. And nobody could steer me with a joystick, because radio signals take minutes to cross from Earth. I had to fly myself.",
